# state: any   (golden 7da19befd45b; lane.savestate433 / lane.profileconv1011)
# NOT PROVEN -- do not read a frame rate off this route. Two proofs on the
# golden (1-1791761288-gtaroutes1011-284417, 1-1791768457-gtaroutes1011-1576234)
# both mount the BMX, then leave CJ in one spot by the alley wall for the whole
# scored window. Neither LY nor A (held or tapped), X or LX moved the bike.
# The input that pedals it on this Xbox port is unknown; see
# docs/lanes/gtaroutes1011/NOTES.md section 10.
# Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas (54540082, USA): a DRIVING route, not the
# on-foot measurement gta-sa.route takes. Same boot (do not edit gta-sa.route
# for this -- today's A/B depends on it; this file copies its beats through
# the point CJ is moved down the Jefferson alley, then diverges): Rockstar
# logos -> intro credits FMV (A skips it) -> title "Press START" (START) ->
# loading screens (~55 s) -> airport cutscene (A skips it) -> police-stop
# cutscene (A skips it) -> Jefferson alley, CJ on foot, HUD (clock, $350,
# radar), "Use the left thumbstick to move Carl".
#
# The two cutscene skips are a train of A presses 5 s apart (as gta-sa.route):
# loading time differs between runs, and an A that lands on a loading screen
# does nothing.
#
# gta-sa.route's own header records the alley prompt this route uses: moving
# CJ down the alley (LY min, 2.2 s) surfaces "Press Y to jump on the bike" --
# the BMX marked with a blue cone, per the brief (step 4). One Y press mounts
# it; `mark gameplay` is set after the mount is on screen, not before, so the
# scored window is riding, not the on-foot walk gta-sa.route already covers.
#
# Player control once mounted: A pedals; the left stick does NOT. The first
# proof (1-1791761288-gtaroutes1011-284417) rode LY min and sat still: the
# mount worked ("BMX" on screen) and the game's own help said "Push up or
# down on the left thumbstick to shift your weight on the bike", and f00009-
# f00020 show CJ on the bike in one spot by the alley wall, radar unchanged.
# So the loop holds A (steady pedalling) and, once a cycle, taps it (the
# faster pedal stroke, and the input that moves the bike if a held A only
# coasts), steers with LX on the pedal, and lets go of A for a short X
# (brake/back) with the bar turned so a wall it rides into cannot hold it.
# Never Y, START or BACK after the mount (another Y would dismount).
#
wait 26.7
shot boot
wait 36.7
press A 300
wait 6.1
shot skA
wait 8.6
press START 300
wait 9.8
shot menu
wait 30.0
shot load
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
shot cut1
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
shot cut2
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
press A 300
wait 5
shot cut3
wait 10
axis LY min
wait 2.2
axis LY mid
shot moved
wait 1
press Y 300
wait 2.5
shot mounted
mark gameplay
hold A
repeat forever {
    wait 3
    axis LX max
    wait 1.2
    axis LX mid
    wait 3
    axis LX min
    wait 1.2
    axis LX mid
    release A
    mash A 8 0.25
    axis LX max
    hold X
    wait 1
    release X
    axis LX mid
    hold A
}
